>>
Rule 1 (Input tensor must have at least two dimensions)
{x : tensor} |= ndim(x) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 3 (The elements in the permutation list must be within the range of the input tensor's dimensions)
{x : tensor, perm : list(int)} |= ∀ i ∈ [0, perm.len - 1] : 0 ≤ perm[i] ∧ perm[i] < ndim(x)
>>
Rule 4 (Permutation list cannot have duplicate elements)
{perm : list(int)} |= ∀ i ∈ [0, perm.len - 1] : ∀ j ∈ [i+1, perm.len - 1] : perm[i] ≠ perm[j]
>>
Rule 5 (Input tensor's datatype cannot be bool)
{x : tensor} |= dtype_(x) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 7 (Check if perm is none if tensor rank is 2)
{x : tensor, perm : list(int)} |= if ndim(x) = 2 then perm = none
>>
Rule 10 (If permutation is not none, the length of permutation must be less than or equal to the rank of the input tensor.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= if v_2 ≠ none then v_2.len ≤ ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 11 (Each element in permutation should be within the range of input tensor's dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : list(int)} |= if v_2 ≠ none then ∀ i ∈ [0, v_2.len - 1] : v_2[i] ≥ 0 ∧ v_2[i] < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 15 (If perm is not none, its length must be less than or equal to the rank of x)
{x : tensor, perm : list(int)} |= if perm ≠ "none" then perm.len ≤ ndim(x)
>>
Rule 16 (If perm is not none, its elements must be valid indices for x's dimensions)
{x : tensor, perm : list(int)} |= if perm ≠ "none" then ∀ i ∈ [0, perm.len - 1] : perm[i] ≥ 0 ∧ perm[i] < ndim(x)
>>
Rule 21 (If 'perm' is "none", then it's okay. Otherwise, if 'perm' is a list, it's length must not exceed the rank of 'x'.)
{x : tensor, perm : list(int) ⊎ str} |= if perm = "none" then true else (if perm ≠ "none" then perm.len ≤ ndim(x) else false)
>>
Rule 27 (If 'perm' is not none then each element in 'perm' must be an integer within the valid dimension range of tensor 'x')
{x : tensor, perm : list(int) ⊎ str} |= if perm ≠ "none" then ∀ i ∈ [0, perm.len - 1] : perm[i] ≥ 0 ∧ perm[i] < ndim(x)
>>
Rule 28 (If 'perm' is not none then the length of 'perm' cannot exceed the number of dimensions of tensor 'x')
{x : tensor, perm : list(int) ⊎ str} |= if perm ≠ "none" then perm.len ≤ ndim(x)
